To terminate a C program, you can use the exit() function from the stdlib.h library or return 0 at the end of your main() function to indicate successful termination. Here's an example:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main()
{
    // Your code here...

    // Terminate the program with success status
    return 0;
}
```

Alternatively, if you want to forcefully terminate the program without returning any value, you can call `exit(1)` (or another non-zero integer) instead of using `return`. This will cause the program to immediately stop executing and

